-- title:
--   Component ideals at the points η(v) of the glued model
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q\nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel.html#L71) (a proper, flat, integral, locally finitely presented model over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation $R=$ [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.R q`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel.html#L32) together with its normality, generic smoothness, function-field and section data). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O\colon R\to O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with a ring map $O\to\kappa$, and assume the site hypotheses $H$: finiteness of the node set, the oriented crossing charts, the étale-neighbourhood datum, injectivity and closedness of the node points in $\mathfrak X_O$, and the model hypotheses on $q$ and $O$. Assume moreover that each $\xi_j$ lies in the open `X0` of the chart input $C$, i.e. off the marked points. Write $Y$ for the glued scheme obtained from this data and $\mathrm{comp}$ for its family of ideal-sheaf data indexed by the component set. The assertion is: for every index $v$ there are an affine open $U$ of $Y$ and a membership $\eta(v)\in U$ such that the image of the ideal $\mathrm{comp}(v)(U)\subseteq\Gamma(Y,U)$ under the germ map to the stalk $\mathcal O_{Y,\eta(v)}$ generates the maximal ideal of that stalk, while for every $w\ne v$ the image of $\mathrm{comp}(w)(U)$ is the unit ideal.
--
--   This records the local behaviour of the component ideal sheaves of the glued resolution at the distinguished points $\eta(v)$: each component cuts out the maximal ideal of the stalk there, and the remaining components do not pass through the point. It feeds into the assembly of the resolved (regular) Deligne–Rapoport model and its charts, [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_V3AsmLevel_eta_stalk.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
